      "Subject rotation stops the child from living in the one subject they like. A simple pattern for a school-day evening: one heavy paper (Mathematics or Science), a short break, one language or Social Studies task. Alternate which heavy paper leads. Saturday can hold a longer mixed set: a timed English composition one week, a timed maths paper the next. Two subjects treated well beat five subjects touched with a highlighter.",
